{
  "_about": [
    "The P4 deck's channels, one view per page (PROTOCOL.md 4.7). The deck declares",
    "every channel below, and on each page change asks the host for just that page's",
    "view, so a page pays only for its own data on the wire. Each list is what that",
    "page's code reads (its TC_CH_* references), so add a channel here in the same",
    "change that makes a page read it.",
    "",
    "'always' rides in every view. It holds what must stay current while its page is",
    "hidden: the history the fps, system and g-force pages draw (their traces and",
    "peaks would otherwise have gaps), and the lap and sector events the timing page",
    "keys its PB flashes and best-before deltas on. Everything else may freeze",
    "off-screen; the deck widens its view to the incoming page before drawing it."
  ],
